    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0071_acabbb4fe40c.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 118px;\" /><br />Equation of the chord of contact&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math><br />According to the property, the chord of contact w.r.t. any point on the directrix always passes through focus <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> i.e., <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> satisfy the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>h</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Length of the latus rectum is <math><mn>8</mn></math></p> units"
